
=== 1. a primary home and a real local secondmate home with a capacity-2 pool ===
primary pool declaration:
  {"pools":[{"name":"shared","capacity":2,"models":["pool-model-a","pool-model-b"]}]}
secondmate binding:
  schema=fm-secondmate-parent.v1
  route=local
  parent_home=/tmp/fm-live-s1.H6EO3Y/primary

=== 2. a launch from the primary takes the first seat ===
fleet-seats: reserved pool=shared id=ship-one generation=gA used=1 capacity=2
rc=0

=== 3. a launch from the secondmate home takes the second seat out of the SAME pool ===
fleet-seats: reserved pool=shared id=ship-two generation=gB used=2 capacity=2
rc=0

=== 4. a third launch from the secondmate home is refused with the shared holders listed ===
fleet-seats: pool shared is full (2 of 2 seats held); ship-three gets no seat for model pool-model-a - choose an overflow route or wait for a holder to finish
  holder /tmp/fm-live-s1.H6EO3Y/mate/state ship-two
  holder /tmp/fm-live-s1.H6EO3Y/primary/state ship-one
rc=4

=== 5. the ledger lives once, at the root, not in the secondmate home ===
2786179283-45.json
791703965-42.json
no ledger of its own in the secondmate home

=== 6. releasing one generation admits exactly one new launch ===
fleet-seats: released id=ship-one generation=gA reason=teardown
fleet-seats: reserved pool=shared id=ship-three generation=gC used=2 capacity=2
retry rc=0

=== 7. adversarial: the same generation cannot be confirmed twice or revived after release ===
fleet-seats: pool shared is full (2 of 2 seats held); ship-four gets no seat for model pool-model-a - choose an overflow route or wait for a holder to finish
  holder /tmp/fm-live-s1.H6EO3Y/mate/state ship-three
  holder /tmp/fm-live-s1.H6EO3Y/mate/state ship-two
reuse-of-released-generation rc=4
fleet-seats: no seat - harness claude launches an unverified default model; pass an explicit --model while fleet seat pools are configured (a pooled model is never launched without a counted seat; choose another route or repair the authority)
unverified-default-model rc=5

=== 8. adversarial: a terminal generation is never revived for the same holder
fleet-seats: refused - generation gA of ship-one is already terminal; a new episode needs a new generation
revive-released-generation rc=5

=== 9. two generations of one holder in one pool count once
fleet-seats: released id=ship-two generation=gB reason=teardown
fleet-seats: reserved pool=shared id=ship-two generation=gB2 used=2 capacity=2
successor rc=0
